                <pb facs="0989" n="893" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg893"/>

                <head>No. 403.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Christianey to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima, Peru</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-08-05"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 5, 1879</date>.
                        (Received September 4.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 46.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that
                    President Prado telegraphs from Iquique that the Chilian fleet has voluntarily
                    raised the blockade of that port, and by a subsequent dispatch he says they are
                    at present in Autafogasta.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>I. P. CHRISTIANCY.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
